WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.560
Swallow flew away from the writer's cottage.

2
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.640
The late autumn wind blew hard and cold.

3
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.960
"It's so hard to fly," Swallow thought.

4
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.540
"I'll rest awhile at the fountain."

5
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.967
He landed and dipped his beak in the fountain.

6
00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:40.204
The water was so cold, it sent a chill down his throat.

7
00:00:40.205 --> 00:00:44.179
"Leader was right," he thought.

8
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:50.380
"It's getting too cold here. Maybe the sun will warm me."

9
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.960
Swallow sat on the fountain's edge, soaking in the weak sunlight.

10
00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.000
Suddenly a dark shadow spilled over him.

11
00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.940
"I saw what you did!" a voice growled.

12
00:01:09.521 --> 00:01:14.746
Swallow looked up. "Oh no! The hawk!"

13
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.430
He flew off in terror, wings flapping wildly.

14
00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.230
But he felt cold, which slowed down his flying.

15
00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:30.830
"Come back!" the hawk screeched. "Come back right now!"

16
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.940
Swallow soared and swooped, zigzagging through the sky.

17
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.787
His heart pounded as he darted between branches and rooftops.

18
00:01:42.788 --> 00:01:50.496
Finally, he spotted a thick bush and dove into it, trembling.

19
00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:54.250
The hawk flew past, missing him completely.

20
00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.860
Safe but scared, Swallow returned to the statue.

21
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:08.270
Curling up at the statue's feet, he tucked his head beneath his wing.

22
00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.310
He fell into a deep sleep.

23
00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:23.080
Swallow flew through the gentle, warm air. "I'm here—Egypt at last!"

24
00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.090
He spotted his flock in a tall tree and flew toward them.

25
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:34.210
But just as he was about to land, the tree disappeared.

26
00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.310
So did his flock.

27
00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.410
A dark fog rolled in, covering the bright sky.

28
00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:49.030
Swallow shivered. "What's happening? Where is everyone?"

29
00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:57.000
"Swallow," a voice called. It was kind and familiar.

30
00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:03.320
"I can hear you," Swallow said. "But I can't see you."

31
00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:10.400
"Swallow," the voice said again. "Swallow, wake up!"

32
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.640
Slowly the bird realized he'd been dreaming.

33
00:03:19.001 --> 00:03:22.162
The voice was the statue's.

34
00:03:22.163 --> 00:03:27.996
Swallow tried to shake off the dream, but his throat ached.

35
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.780
His feathers were cold and wet.

36
00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:41.537
"Oh, my poor friend." The statue sighed.

37
00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:49.010
"It is too cold for you here. Go now, fly to Egypt, where it's warm."

38
00:03:50.121 --> 00:03:54.909
"I'm too weak," Swallow whispered.

39
00:03:55.350 --> 00:04:00.370
"I'm going to another place now—the land beyond life."

40
00:04:03.372 --> 00:04:09.777
"No! Please, don't die!" the statue begged.

41
00:04:09.778 --> 00:04:15.787
Swallow lay still, barely moving.

42
00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.880
The statue cried and cried.

43
00:04:23.285 --> 00:04:28.204
"If only I were a prince again," he thought.

44
00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:35.330
"I could help him. Blast this terrible curse and my unloving heart!"

45
00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:41.090
As the statue continued to cry, a puddle formed at his base.
